{"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:15GraphOperations12SubgraphViewV","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SubgraphView.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView.swift#L29"},"roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"title":"SubgraphView","symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"GraphOperations"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"densely. Made by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inducedSubgraph(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spanningSubgraph(edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraph(vertices:edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraph_view"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsSubgraph"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SubDigraph"},{"type":"text","text":", Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"filtered_graph"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertices"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" are the kept vertices in the base’s order, at view indices ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"view keeps two arrays, base index to view index and back, so a row is the base’s row filtered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and renumbered with one array load per entry and no hashing. A spanning subgraph keeps every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex at its base index.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" keep the base’s positions, so a weight closure keyed by the base’s positions works","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on the view. An edge is in the view when both its ends are, and, if an edge set was given,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when it is in the set. With an edge set the view has dense edge indices: an edge’s index is its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rank among the kept edges in base order. Over a base with edge indices the set is a bit mask","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a count per 64-bit word, so the rank costs one popcount. Over a base without them (an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a complement, an induced subgraph) the set is the sorted kept positions, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a row entry or a rank costs a binary search. An induced subgraph has no edge indices: building","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its edge mask would cost O(m). One on every vertex keeps the base’s rows, edge indices and flat","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rows.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The view holds a copy of the base (value semantics), so mutating the original never shows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through. Phase 1 needs a base with vertex indices; a ","type":"text"},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with vertex holes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"traps at construction.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations"]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeIndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/base"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview"]}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","title":"DirectedGraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphOperations/s9EscapableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","title":"Swift.Escapable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView":{"abstract":[{"text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"densely. Made by ","type":"text"},{"code":"inducedSubgraph(on:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"spanningSubgraph(edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"subgraph(vertices:edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (NetworkX’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"subgraph_view","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", JGraphT’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsSubgraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", LEMON’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SubDigraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"filtered_graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"title":"SubgraphView","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/BidirectionalDirectedGraph":{"title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph that also answers in-neighborhoods: Boost’s "},{"code":"BidirectionalGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Kept apart"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" because in-adjacency usually costs extra storage, and many algorithms only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"go forward."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/DirectedGraph-Implementations":{"role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/directedgraph-implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","title":"Direc